evd-fortran is a modern Fortran translation of computational routines from
the R package evd 2.3-7.1 by Alec Stephenson. The upstream package is licensed
GPL-3 and identifies Chris Ferro as the author of function fbvpot.

Upstream citation:
A. G. Stephenson (2002), "evd: Extreme Value Distributions", R News 2(2), 31-32.

The simulation routines for logistic/asymmetric-logistic models retain the
upstream comments identifying Algorithms 1.1, 1.2, 2.1 and 2.2 of Stephenson
(2003). The numerical/statistical formulas are derived from the corresponding
GPL-3 R/C source files included in the upstream release.

src/r_mod.f90 is the separately supplied MIT-licensed compatibility helper and
is covered by LICENSES/r_mod-MIT.txt. All evd-derived translation files are
covered by LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt.
